  "physical_interpretation": "In Singh 2016 Table 1 for 131Ce, authors visually summarize a Qt drop from ~3 eb at low spin to ~2.5 eb at high spin. Our rigorous weighted regression on the four finite data points (15/2-, 27/2-, 31/2-, 35/2-) gives a slope of -0.0302 +/- 0.0472 eb/hbar, which is only a 0.64-sigma effect (under 1-sigma). A constant Qt model with weighted mean 2.58 +/- 0.10 eb yields chi2/dof = 0.89, which is statistically fully acceptable. All three unilateral limits (19/2-, 23/2-, 39/2-) are completely consistent with this constant mean. Furthermore, the side-feeding treatment changes qualitatively across the spin sequence: at 15/2- and 27/2- a constant delay tau_SF (0.7-1.0 ps) is used, whereas at 31/2- and 35/2- a collective rotational cascade Q_SF (~5-6 eb) is fitted. Because side-feeding models trade off directly against the fitted lifetime, the visual Qt drop could easily arise from the shift in side-feeding parametrization rather than an intrinsic nuclear deformation change. This provides a textbook Day 18 audit example of how feeding model choices and limited statistical significance affect high-spin shape conclusions."
